| info = 
*Nekros expends {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''100''' [[energy]] to summon <u>'''4 / 5 / 6 / 7'''</u> shadow copies of his most recently slain enemies, prioritizing the strongest enemy groups among those killed to summon. The copies retain the level and stats of their original selves but will gain {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''25% / 50% / 75% / 150%''' damage, {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''15% / 35% / 65% / 100%''' shields and {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''15% / 35% / 65% / 100%''' health, with each copy losing {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''3%''' of their health per second while active. 
**Shadows spawn around Nekros in a clockwise fashion, within a '''10''' meter radius.
***High priority enemies will spawn first, enemies of equal priority will appear in order of deaths.
***Spawn order starts from the direction where the player's camera is looking, but the Shadows themselves face the same direction as Nekros.
**Shadows of the Dead's damage, shield and health bonuses '''multiply''' a Shadow's total damage, shield and health. For example, +30% Ability Strength will increase the damage and health bonuses to {{Math|1.5 {{mul}} 1.3|mt=y|percent=y}} and {{Math|1 {{mul}} 1.3|mt=y|percent=y}} respectively at max rank. A copy whose original had 200 total health and dealt 100 damage per attack will have {{Math|200 {{mul}} (1 + 1.3)|mt=y}} health when summoned and will inflict {{Math|100 {{mul}} (1 + 1.95)|mt=y}} damage per attack.
**There is currently no way to prematurely kill shadows in order to refresh them, either the shadows or Nekros must die in order for this to happen.
**The number of active Shadows is displayed on the ability icon.
***Shadows of enemies that summon additional units, like {{E|Drahk Master}}s, can summon Shadows of their respective minions. These can exceed the number of Shadows Nekros can normally summon, and will be reflected in the number on the ability icon. They also contribute extra damage reduction when {{M|Shield of Shadows}} is equipped.
**Shadows can be healed with some [[Healing]] mods, abilities, arcanes, weapons, and allied Shadows' abilities (e.g. {{E|Aerolyst}} canisters/sparks, [[Leech Eximus]] damage zone, etc.). Some shadows also can'''not''' die.
***This can become a problem later on when the Nekros player needs to refresh their shadows to get higher level versions, but cannot do so until they die. 
*Has a very long cast animation, during which Shadows usually will not attack. Nekros is '''not''' immune to knockdown and takes full damage during this time.
*Casting the ability again (default {{Keybind|4}}) while there are Shadows still active performs additional functions:
**Active Shadows that are more than <u>'''30'''</u> meters away from Nekros will teleport into Nekros' spawn radius.
**Fully replenishes active Shadows' shields and health on each recast. If the number of active Shadows are at maximum capacity, Nekros will perform a shortened animation.
***Shadows are '''not''' healed before the completion of the animation; as such, if recasting at maximum Shadows, some can die before getting healed, and more will '''not''' be spawned to compensate.
**When the number of active Shadows falls below the maximum, Nekros performs the full summoning animation to create additional Shadows up to the maximum capacity. 
***This function can only be performed when there are slain enemies in Nekros's "recently-killed" list (see [[#Summoning Priority]]).
*Dying or experiencing a host migration will destroy any Shadows you currently had stored.
*Shadows are selectively summoned and possess unique properties:
