{{!}}-{{!}}Shadow Quirks=
This is a list of strange properties unique to specific Shadows. See also: [[#Shadow Properties]].
*Some Shadows have a '''very''' slow decay rate compared to others (potentially via passive regeneration): {{E|Deimos Therid}}, {{E|Manic Bombard}}, and {{E|Ghoul Rictus Alpha}}.
*Some Shadows can spawn <u>allied non-Shadow units</u>, these units collide with players, do '''not''' increase the Shadow count, do '''not''' contribute to {{M|Shield of Shadows}}, and do '''not''' decay. See [[#Bugs]] for more details.
*Some Shadows will '''not''' use their abilities or gear. See [[#Bugs]] for more details.
*A {{E|Drahk Master}} will '''not''' disarm enemies.
*{{E|Amalgam Heqet}}, {{E|Amalgam Arca Heqet}}, and {{E|Amalgam Osprey}} will '''not''' create a {{E|Spectralyst}}.
*A {{E|Spectralyst}} will '''not''' retain the loadout it copied, the Shadow will use the base loadout.
*A dying {{E|Thrax Legatus}} or {{E|Thrax Centurion}} will '''not''' become incorporeal.
*A decayed or killed {{E|Eidolon Vomvalyst}} will become incorporeal instead of dying.
**If an {{E|Eidolon Lure}} is tethered to such Shadow - it will be charged, and the Shadow will be consumed.
*A {{E|Tusk Dargyn}}/{{E|Tusk Shield Dargyn}} Shadow spawns complete with a {{E|Dargyn Pilot}} model, can fly like normal, and counts as '''1''' Shadow.
**Upon death it will spawn a {{E|Dargyn Pilot}} '''enemy'''.
**Killing an empty or unmarked {{E|Tusk Dargyn}}/{{E|Tusk Shield Dargyn}} will '''not''' create a Shadow.
*A {{E|Mimic}} will spawn disguised and will reveal itself '''only''' when approached by a player.
**It will occasionally try to move away from players and into another room, to disguise itself.
*{{E|Kosma Gokstad Officer}}, {{E|Anarch Grineer Trapper}}, and {{E|Summulyst}} will deploy allied drones, which are '''not''' Shadows and will '''not''' die when their master dies.
**Same thing happens with [[Tech]]s, {{E|Vapos Tech Ranger}}, {{E|Corrupted MOA}}, and {{E|Fusion MOA}} except their drones will die.
*A dying {{E|Mitosid}} will split into allied {{E|Basal Diploid}} and {{E|Feral Diploid}}, which are '''not''' Shadows.
*A {{E|Mutalist Osprey}} will spawn complete with a {{E|Crawler}} Shadow level '''1''' and drop it.
**It will not pick up {{E|Crawler}}s.
*A {{E|Deimos Tendril Drone}} will '''not''' face-hug enemies.
*A dying {{E|Deimos Undying Flyer}} will deploy a pod, which is immediately destroyed (probably by the Shadow decay).
*An {{E|Anarch Grineer Lancer}} will occasionally become a suicide bomber, even <u>with no enemy presence</u> (probably because of the Shadow decay).
*An {{E|Anarch Tenebra}} will open enemies up to [[Ground Finisher]]s with its lurk attack.
*A {{E|Scaldra Barbican}}'s shield can break with enough damage.
}}
<hr/>
*'''Ability Synergy:''' A target killed by {{A|Soul Punch}} summons a friendly {{A|Shadows of the Dead}} copy of the enemy target. If the target survives, they become Marked for Harvest for <u>'''3'''</u> seconds, creating their Shadow if killed while marked.
**If the max Shadows count is reached, all active Shadows are healed to full health instead.
**If {{A|Shadows of the Dead}} was subsumed over, the Shadows do '''not''' receive bonus stats.
**Enemies with {{D|Overguard}} can'''not''' be marked.
